IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`

-- Tests for the date helpers in spr-dates.l4.
-- These helpers are counting conventions (fork register F1 to F4), not provisions of
-- the Regulations, so the expected values are worked out by hand from the convention
-- stated beside each helper, not from the text of the Regulations.

§ `F1: N days starting with D (inclusive)`

-- 28 days starting with 1 March 2020: 1 March is day 1, so day 28 is 28 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days starting with` (YMD 2020 3 1) 28 EQUALS YMD 2020 3 28
-- One day starting with D is D itself.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days starting with` (YMD 2020 3 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2020 3 1
-- Across a month end: 28 days starting with 15 February 2020 (a leap year) end on 13 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days starting with` (YMD 2020 2 15) 28 EQUALS YMD 2020 3 13

§ `F2: N months starting on D`

-- 3 months starting on 15 January 2020 end on 14 April 2020.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months starting on` (YMD 2020 1 15) 3 EQUALS YMD 2020 4 14
-- 12 months starting on 15 March 2020 end on 14 March 2021.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months starting on` (YMD 2020 3 15) 12 EQUALS YMD 2021 3 14
-- 1 month starting on 1 March ends on 31 March (the day before the corresponding date, 1 April).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months starting on` (YMD 2020 3 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2020 3 31
-- Month-end start, no corresponding date: 1 month starting on 31 January 2021 ends on the
-- last day of February 2021, which is 28 February (convention F2, not stated in the text).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months starting on` (YMD 2021 1 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2021 2 28

§ `F3: tax years run from 6 April to 5 April`

#ASSERT `the tax year in which the day falls` (YMD 2016 4 6) EQUALS 2016
#ASSERT `the tax year in which the day falls` (YMD 2016 4 5) EQUALS 2015
#ASSERT `the tax year in which the day falls` (YMD 2017 1 1) EQUALS 2016
#ASSERT `the tax year in which the day falls` (YMD 2017 12 31) EQUALS 2017
#ASSERT `the first day of the tax year` 2016 EQUALS YMD 2016 4 6
#ASSERT `the last day of the tax year` 2016 EQUALS YMD 2017 4 5

§ `F4: whole days between two dates`

#ASSERT `the number of days from` (YMD 2020 2 1) `to` (YMD 2020 3 1) EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the number of days from` (YMD 2021 2 1) `to` (YMD 2021 3 1) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the number of days from` (YMD 2020 3 1) `to` (YMD 2020 3 1) EQUALS 0

§ `The earlier of two dates`

#ASSERT `the earlier of` (YMD 2020 3 1) `and` (YMD 2020 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 1
#ASSERT `the earlier of` (YMD 2020 3 2) `and` (YMD 2020 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 1
#ASSERT `the earlier of` (YMD 2020 3 1) `and` (YMD 2020 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 1
